// TEST: Unknown Unit Name In Compound Annotation (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3015
// The annotation twin of 048: a name inside a COMPOUND unit annotation must
// resolve. Only a numeric literal may appear undeclared (`Float<1/second>`);
// an identifier has to name something already in scope. Previously this
// degraded to the BARE type, which is worse than the declaration-site
// fallback -- `v` carried no unit at all, so the `Float64<meter>` binding
// below accepted it and every later check on `v` passed too.
Unit meter
Unit second
let v: Float64<meter / secnd> = 3.0
let m: Float64<meter> = v
